Fix bottom nav clipping on narrow phone viewports

The dock was centered with left-1/2 + -translate-x-1/2 and had no
width constraint, so the fifth nav item pushed it past a 320px
viewport and it overflowed both edges with no way to scroll into view.

- Center with inset-x-0 + flex justify-center px-3 instead of a transform
- Add w-fit max-w-full so the pill is bounded by the container
- Tighten padding, gaps, and icon size below the sm breakpoint
- Hide the brand logo on the narrowest screens to reclaim width
- Hide hover tooltips on touch and add aria-label to each link

Dock measures ~224px at 320px wide, leaving ~72px of headroom.

